const r = await tools.exec_command({
  cmd: "gh issue create --title 'Travel Guide Playwright check intermittently captures an unnamed 404' --label tooling --body 'Found by the verifier while running the full suite for #74 checkout-scoped holds. The checkout diff does not touch the Travel Guide journey.\\n\\n## Where\\n\\n`e2e/travelguide.spec.ts:24-28,85` records every browser console error in `renderingErrors` and expects the array to stay empty. One full-suite run captured only:\\n\\n```text\\nFailed to load resource: the server responded with a status of 404 ()\\n```\\n\\nThe console message did not identify the resource.\\n\\n## Reproduction evidence\\n\\n- first full Playwright run: Travel Guide failed; suite 38 passed, 1 failed\\n- isolated `e2e/travelguide.spec.ts` rerun: 1/1 passed\\n- second full Playwright run: 39/39 passed\\n- rate observed: 1 of 2 full runs; 0 of 1 isolated runs\\n\\nA transient server `ECONNRESET` / `Error: aborted` also appeared elsewhere in the first full run, but did not fail a test and its relationship to this 404 is unknown.\\n\\n## Why it matters\\n\\nThe test is intentionally a rendered-error guard, so ignoring the 404 would weaken it. Until the missing resource or server timing is identified, healthy pull requests can fail nondeterministically and a real rendering regression is indistinguishable from environment noise.\\n\\nVerified against the running application; the source of the 404 remains unconfirmed.'",
